WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.889
They're the unhailed heroes of Hollywood:
stunt doubles.

00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:08.320
From free falls of fifty feet or more to crashing
through windows, amazing chase scenes and

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.250
incredible choreographed fights, stunt doubles
make most of the silver screen's biggest blockbusters

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.250
possible.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.230
Here's a peek at what they really look like,
and more about their amazing stunt resumes.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.880
Tanoai Reed is Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.320
The Rock's cousin Tanoai Reed has worked as
his stunt double in nearly 20 different roles.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.770
From 2002's The Scorpion King to 2017's Baywatch,
Reed has been performing stunts for his world

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:31.770
famous cuz.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.650
In addition to being practically as close
as brothers, Reed and Johnson frequently collaborate

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.470
behind-the-scenes on aspects of their combined
performance.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:42.730
Reed has won two Taurus World Stunt awards
over the years for his work, as well as working

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:48.260
as an actor and motion-capture performer for
the 2011 video game Thor: God of Thunder.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.550
Paul Darnell is Robert Pattinson

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.210
For the last ten years, Paul Darnell has been
working as a stuntman — when he's not busy

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.340
competing in parkour and freerunning competitions
around the world.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.250
Darnell was inspired to start freerunning
and doing stunt work after watching a 2003

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.570
episode of Ripley's Believe it or Not! which
featured parkour.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:08.700
Not only is a talented stuntman, but Darnell
has also been a two-time finalist on the popular

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.060
television series American Ninja Warrior.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:15.070
A former gymnastics champion at Virginia Tech,
Darnell has built up an impressive stunt reel

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:19.020
over the years for himself, including his
work as a double for Henry Cavill in Man of

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.710
Steel, Adam Sandler in You Don't Mess with
the Zohan, Paul Walker in Fast Five, and Robert

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:28.450
Pattinson in Water for Elephants, Remember
Me, and the Twilight saga — a gig that Pattinson

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.730
thanked Darnell for when the film won "Best
Fight" at the MTV Movie Awards.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.080
Marny Eng is Reese Witherspoon

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.120
Since the early 1990s, Canadian stuntwoman
Marny Eng has racked up more than 100 roles

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.030
working as a stunt double and stunt coordinator,
and has been twice nominated for a Taurus

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.490
World Stunt Award, among many others.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.000
She's doubled for dozens of women and men
over the years, but the actress she's performed

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.490
stunts for most frequently has been Reese
Witherspoon.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:55.770
Eng has been her double in at least three
different roles, including 2015's Hot Pursuit.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:59.729
Eng is also no stranger to acting, and you
can spot her as Tabitha — a spoof of the

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:04.920
character Samara from The Ring — in the
2003 horror comedy Scary Movie 3.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.740
Jack Gill is Will Ferrell

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.090
There's no question that the hilarious NASCAR
comedy Talladega Nights: The Ballad of Ricky

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:14.750
Bobby required a lot of fancy stunt driving,
and Jack Gill is the man behind that action.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:19.310
Since the 1970s, Gill has worked as a stunt
performer and stunt driver on over 170 films

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.620
and television shows, including as the primary
stunt driver on both The Dukes of Hazzard

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:24.620
and Knight Rider.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.560
"We had a good time on the show and it was
one of those types of shows that was like

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.560
a family.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.560
A really tight-knit group."

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.380
Over the years, Gill has branched out into
stunt coordination and second unit directing,

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.420
including on several of the Fast and Furious
films.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.720
With a metal plate in his neck, 23 broken
bones, and eight concussions over the course

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.030
of his four-decade career, there's unquestionably
nobody more qualified than Gill to testify

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.640
about the difficulties of the job.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.151
Gill has also been instrumental in the push
among the stunt community for an Oscar or

00:02:48.151 --> 00:02:51.599
two recognizing the achievements of the stunt
men and women that make so many of today's

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:53.310
movies possible.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.560
Luci Romberg is Melissa McCarthy

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.560
For the last decade, Luci Romberg has been
at the top of her game as a stuntwoman.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.870
The Hollywood native is a former champion
gymnast and also competes as one of the few

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.860
females in high-level freerunning competitions
around the world.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.380
"Fell in love with it and haven't gone back."

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.410
Over the course of her career, Romberg has
doubled for Melissa McCarthy several times,

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.239
including in Identity Thief, Spy, The Boss,
and Ghostbusters.

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:20.430
Greg Fitzpatrick is Ben Stiller

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.989
In the world of stunt performers, getting
a job as the preferred stuntman or woman for

00:03:23.989 --> 00:03:26.780
one of Hollywood's top stars is the ultimate
gig.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.569
For Greg Fitzpatrick, that opportunity came
relatively early in his career, when he was

00:03:30.569 --> 00:03:34.530
picked as the stunt double for Ben Stiller
in the 2003 film Duplex.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.709
Since then, Greg has become the preferred
double for Stiller, and has since appeared

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:40.080
in more than a dozen films as Stiller's stuntman.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.910
In addition to his resemblance to Ben Stiller,
Fitzpatrick is also a talented stunt performer

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.740
and coordinator — he's won two Taurus World
Stunt Awards and doubled for Robert Downey

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.910
Jr. in both Iron Man and Iron Man 2.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:53.970
"I'm so happy to be working — to be allowed
to work in a business that I love.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.760
And I just want to continue to do it."

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.599
Vic Armstrong is Harrison Ford

00:03:58.599 --> 00:04:02.239
According to the Guinness Book of World Records,
Vic Armstrong reigns as the most prolific

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:03.470
stuntman in the world.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.769
Additionally, Armstrong is one of the few
stunt performers to ever break the Academy

00:04:06.769 --> 00:04:10.830
Award barrier, winning a Technical Achievement
Academy Award in 2001.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.800
With well over 100 stunt credits in a career
that spans five decades, it probably would

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.560
not surprise you to learn that Armstrong doubled
for some of Hollywood's biggest roles, including

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.749
as James Bond, Superman, and Indiana Jones.

00:04:20.749 --> 00:04:23.949
"I'm not into drugs or anything, but when
people talk about a high, you do stunts you

00:04:23.949 --> 00:04:29.400
get a natural high that I guarantee you nobody
in the world can match."

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.520
Reportedly, crew members frequently confused
Armstrong with Harrison Ford on the set of

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:37.120
the Indiana Jones films, which resulted in
Ford sending Armstrong a photo of the two

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.129
of them with the humorous inscription, "If
you learn to talk, I'm in deep trouble!"

00:04:41.129 --> 00:04:43.009
Billy Lucas is Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:04:43.009 --> 00:04:47.389
Since 1990's Total Recall, stuntman Billy
Lucas has had the sweet gig of working as

00:04:47.389 --> 00:04:50.550
Arnold Schwarzenegger's stunt double on the
set of most of his films.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.610
From Kindergarten Cop to the Terminator series,
if you saw Arnold do some crazy action scenes,

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:58.560
it was most likely Lucas' work that you were
watching, not Arnold's:

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:07.819
In addition to his roles as Schwarzenegger's
stunt double, Lucas has worked on over 100

00:05:07.819 --> 00:05:10.889
different movies and TV shows as a stunt performer
and coordinator.

00:05:10.889 --> 00:05:14.349
Despite his undoubtedly busy schedule, it
seems that Schwarzenegger and Lucas have become

00:05:14.349 --> 00:05:17.910
close over the years — the former California
Governor even shared a story of how Lucas

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:22.289
saved his life during a risky scuba-diving
shot on the set of The 6th Day, saying "I

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:23.289
was trapped.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.449
Then a hand grabbed me and pulled me out.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:25.969
It was my stunt double, Billy Lucas.

00:05:25.969 --> 00:05:29.741
He'd been watching from below with a tank
and goggles and realised I was in big, big

00:05:29.741 --> 00:05:31.069
trouble."

00:05:31.069 --> 00:05:32.409
Randolph LeRoi is Will Smith

00:05:32.409 --> 00:05:36.999
A Haitian native who immigrated to Brooklyn
as a child, Randolph LeRoi grew up playing

00:05:36.999 --> 00:05:38.930
sports and training in taekwondo.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:42.869
As an adult, LeRoi got involved in modeling
and also became a firefighter in Miami.

00:05:42.869 --> 00:05:46.469
A spot as "Mr. May" on the fire department's
promotional calendar began to land him roles

00:05:46.469 --> 00:05:50.490
in commercials and TV spots in Florida, which
prompted LeRoi to move to California to try

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.379
his hand at acting and stunt performing.

00:05:52.379 --> 00:05:56.539
After being picked as the stunt double for
Will Smith on 1995's Bad Boys, LeRoi and Smith

00:05:56.539 --> 00:05:57.999
have become close friends.

00:05:57.999 --> 00:06:02.909
Since then, LeRoi has doubled for Smith on
nearly a dozen films, like in 2007's I am

00:06:02.909 --> 00:06:03.909
Legend.

00:06:03.909 --> 00:06:05.279
Eddie Yansick is Nicolas Cage

00:06:05.279 --> 00:06:09.710
Only a few short years after his stuntman
debut in 1993, Eddie Yansick got picked to

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:13.430
be Nicolas Cage's stunt double in the 1997
action film Con Air.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:17.180
Since then, Yansick has doubled for Cage in
more than a dozen roles, including Lord of

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.039
War, Matchstick Men, and Ghost Rider.

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:22.960
In addition to his over 70 stunt credits over
the last three decades, Yansick also works

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.789
as a stunt coordinator, actor, and a second
unit director.

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:29.839
In 2001, Yansick distinguished himself with
his stunt work when he won a Taurus award

00:06:29.839 --> 00:06:33.460
for best driving for his performance in a
Gone in Sixty Seconds chase scene between

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.439
a Mustang and a police car.

00:06:35.439 --> 00:06:37.339
Tony Angelotti is Johnny Depp

00:06:37.339 --> 00:06:40.680
Tony Angelotti is primarily known for his
work as Johnny Depp's stunt double in the

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.990
Pirates of the Caribbean film franchise, a
job he's held at significant personal cost.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:49.649
An accident on the set of Dead Man's Chest
in 2005 nearly ended his career — and his

00:06:49.649 --> 00:06:50.649
life.

00:06:50.649 --> 00:06:53.369
While rehearsing a "human yo-yo" stunt, everything
went drastically wrong …

00:06:53.369 --> 00:06:54.369
"Whoa!

00:06:54.369 --> 00:06:56.490
Oh s--- ! Oh!

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.490
Oh my God!

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.490
Ow!

00:06:58.490 --> 00:06:59.490
Oh!

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.490
Oh!

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.490
Get me down!"]

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:02.689
… the tension on the line was incorrect,
and the centrifugal force whipped him around

00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:06.360
so hard that when Angelotti hit the end of
the line, his pelvis was split apart like

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.699
a wishbone on a turkey.

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:11.559
It may not look that bad, but while prepping
this sequence, Angelotti broke his pelvis,

00:07:11.559 --> 00:07:15.490
suffered injuries to his knees, legs, and
bladder, and lost a massive six units of blood

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:16.550
from internal bleeding.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:18.330
But he hasn't let his injuries keep him down.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:22.969
He doubled again for Depp in 2007's At World's
End, and continues to work in the stunt field

00:07:22.969 --> 00:07:23.969
today.

00:07:23.969 --> 00:07:24.969
But not every stunt performer can walk away
from injuries and return to the job.

00:07:24.969 --> 00:07:26.119
Olivia Jackson is Milla Jovovich

00:07:26.119 --> 00:07:30.569
Olivia Jackson's promising stunt career was
cut short in 2016 when she suffered a near-fatal

00:07:30.569 --> 00:07:34.869
accident on the set of Resident Evil: The
Final Chapter, where she was working as Milla

00:07:34.869 --> 00:07:35.869
Jovovich's stunt double.

00:07:35.869 --> 00:07:39.319
Prior to her role in that film, Jackson had
worked as the stunt double for Charlize Theron

00:07:39.319 --> 00:07:43.599
in Mad Max: Fury Road and for Elizabeth Olsen
in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:07:43.599 --> 00:07:47.029
In the horrific incident, the motorcycle that
Jackson was riding in a scene crashed into

00:07:47.029 --> 00:07:50.969
a camera crane arm when it malfunctioned and
didn't move out of the way fast enough.

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:54.839
Jackson was in a medically-induced coma for
17 days because of her injuries, which included

00:07:54.839 --> 00:07:58.999
serious facial trauma, a punctured lung, a
crushed arm which had to be amputated, and

00:07:58.999 --> 00:08:00.979
debilitating damage to her spine and neck.

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:04.099
The accident wouldn't be the only incident
to plague the set of Resident Evil — not

00:08:04.099 --> 00:08:07.439
long after Jackson's crash, a crew member
on the set died when a Humvee slipped from

00:08:07.439 --> 00:08:09.150
a sling and crushed him beneath.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.610
For her part, Jackson is fighting bravely
to move on with her life, and recently shared

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:15.110
some photos of herself on the road to recovery.

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.110
Thanks for watching!

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.009
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:18.009 --> 00:08:20.199
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

